    "id": "2100474654301581364",
    "text": "Despite its name, Arab Light crude is not really a light crude. (Why are oil markets so darn confusing?)\n\nSo please don't think we can replace Arab Light directly with other light sweet crudes. The lower residue yield from the lighter crudes will be insufficient to load up the secondary units such as the FCC or cokers.\n\nThese grades from the attached chart are more suitable.\n\nTo take the lighter grades (like WTI and CPC), some blending will be required with heavier grades.\n\nMore details in the report link below.\n\n#oott",
